                    "checked": false,
                    "text": "Social science and humanities introductions often have a similar three-move structure to that of natural sciences. However, the introduction is likely to be more discursive, with extended descriptions and examples to establish the context of the research. There is more flexibility in the sequence of moves. A wider range of steps is also found.",
